    "en": {
      "title": "Basel Framework: CRE30.31",
      "summary": "CRE30.31 makes top-down eligibility for recourse receivables depend on a 'primary protection' test said to be set in CRE34.4-34.7, but those paragraphs contain no such test.",
      "impact": "Position: Pool of corporate receivables with 20% recourse to the seller Reading a: Apply CRE34.4-34.7: no test, eligibility undeterminable Reading b: Eligibility judged by supervisor on general criteria Difference: Top-down vs bottom-up/F-IRB treatment",
      "correction": "Clarify or correct the cited passage so that the rule and its references give one result for the stated case."
    }
  },
